WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.680
Before you calculate anything, understand where each number comes from.

2
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:10.112
In this lesson, you will learn to read how sales, discounts, costs and profit

3
00:00:10.112 --> 00:00:16.320
connect, check a calculation by hand, and then build a custom column from two existing columns.

4
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.260
Let's think like an analyst!

5
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.538
Let's study the Financial Sample columns one by one:

6
00:00:24.538 --> 00:00:29.840
Manufacturing Price, Sale Price, Gross Sales, Discounts, Sales, COGS, and Profit.

7
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:34.224
Gross Sales is units sold times sale price.

8
00:00:34.224 --> 00:00:38.642
Click a value, and Power Query shows it at the bottom of the screen,

9
00:00:38.642 --> 00:00:40.220
so you can check it.

10
00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:53.938
Sales is Gross Sales minus Discounts.

11
00:00:53.938 --> 00:00:58.040
When the discount is zero, the two values are the same.

12
00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:04.243
COGS means cost of goods sold.

13
00:01:04.243 --> 00:01:07.210
And Profit is Sales minus COGS. Watch:

14
00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:08.905
some profits are negative.

15
00:01:08.905 --> 00:01:10.600
Those products lost money.

16
00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:33.321
Checking a few rows by hand builds trust in your data.

17
00:01:33.321 --> 00:01:37.600
If the numbers don't match, find out why before you build any report.

18
00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:56.355
Now, a new calculation.

19
00:01:56.355 --> 00:01:59.666
On the Add Column tab, click Custom Column.

20
00:01:59.666 --> 00:02:03.805
If the formula box is empty, Power Query tells you:

21
00:02:03.805 --> 00:02:05.460
the formula is incomplete.

22
00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:17.932
I name the column Profit one, and write:

23
00:02:17.932 --> 00:02:19.952
Profit divided by Manufacturing Price.

24
00:02:19.952 --> 00:02:24.800
Use the Insert button, so the column names are spelled exactly right.

25
00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:31.112
No syntax errors detected.

26
00:02:31.112 --> 00:02:35.700
Click OK, and the new column appears at the end of the table.

27
00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:53.495
I move it next to Profit, and check a few rows.

28
00:02:53.495 --> 00:02:54.875
Read, check, then calculate.

29
00:02:54.875 --> 00:02:56.600
That is the analyst's way!

